---
title: "FIG. 4 — Deferred FEC Configuration Merge Sequence"
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant FFmpeg as FFmpeg Encoder
    participant Catalog as Catalog Object
    participant Pending as pending_video_fec
    participant Rendition as Video Rendition

    Note over Catalog: No renditions exist yet

    FFmpeg->>Catalog: set_video_repair_track("video/repair")
    Catalog->>Pending: repair_track = "video/repair"
    Note over Pending: {repair_track: "video/repair"}

    FFmpeg->>Catalog: set_video_fec_config("raptorq", 32, 8, 1312, 133)
    Catalog->>Pending: MERGE algorithm, K, P, T, depth<br/>(preserves existing repair_track)
    Note over Pending: {algorithm: "raptorq",<br/>sourceSymbols: 32,<br/>repairSymbols: 8,<br/>symbolSize: 1312,<br/>interleaveDepthMs: 133,<br/>repair_track: "video/repair"} ✓

    FFmpeg->>Catalog: set_video_codec("video", "avc1.42c01e")
    Catalog->>Rendition: ensure_video("video") creates rendition
    Catalog->>Pending: Clone pending to rendition.fec
    Note over Rendition: video.fec = {algorithm: "raptorq",<br/>sourceSymbols: 32, repairSymbols: 8,<br/>symbolSize: 1312, interleaveDepthMs: 133,<br/>repair_track: "video/repair"} ✓

    Note over Catalog: Subsequent renditions also<br/>get pending FEC (clone, not take)

    FFmpeg->>Catalog: set_video_codec("video-hd", "avc1.640028")
    Catalog->>Rendition: ensure_video("video-hd") creates rendition
    Catalog->>Pending: Clone pending to rendition.fec
    Note over Rendition: video-hd.fec = same config ✓
